 ],
 "answer_text": "Found 1 organism taxon record for CFTR: Homo sapiens [4]. \n\nThe gene symbol is CFTR [1], and the gene name is also CFTR [2]. The gene encodes a member of the ATP-binding cassette transporter superfamily that functions as a chloride channel, controlling ion and water secretion and absorption in epithelial tissues, and mutations in this gene cause cystic fibrosis [3]. \n\nThese annotations are consistent with the gene's described role in epithelial ion and water movement [3]. \n\nOrganism taxon records found\n\nOrganismTaxon NCBITaxon:9606, name: Homo sapiens [4]. \n\nGene records found\n\nGene symbol: CFTR [1]. Gene name: CFTR [2]. \n\nPubmed records found\n\nPubmed title: Molecular Structure of the Human CFTR Ion Channel [5]. Pubmed title: ECFS standards of care on CFTR-related disorders: Diagnostic criteria of CFTR dysfunction [9]. Pubmed title: ECFS standards of care on CFTR-related disorders: Updated diagnostic criteria [12]. Pubmed title: Molecular structures reveal synergistic rescue of \u0394508 CFTR by Trikafta modulators [15]. Pubmed title: In vitro modulator responsiveness of 655 CFTR variants found in people with cystic fibrosis [18]. \n\nClinvar records found\n\nClinvar title: NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1209+1988_1392+2067inv [6]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4(CFTR):c.1392+2072_1392+2074del [10]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.165-291_1585-8528delinsATTTATTCCAAGGGAATAATAAAATAAATAATAATAATA [13]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.2619+2288_2989-839delinsATTAATAATAATAAAT [16]. Clinvar title: NM_000492.4:c.(164+1_165-1)_(1584+1_1585-1)del [19]. \n\nOmim records found\n\nCYSTIC FIBROSIS TRANSMEMBRANE CONDUCTANCE REGULATOR [7]. CFTR [7]. \n\nClinical trial records found\n\nClinical trial name: NPDT Evaluation in Children With CFTR and (PSC) [8]. Clinical trial name: Study of VX-809 in Cystic Fibrosis Subjects With the \u2206F508-CFTR Gene Mutation [11]. Clinical trial name: Detection of Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Conductance Regulator (CFTR) Activity in Rectal Tissues From Human Subjects [14]. Clinical trial name: Effects of Sildenafil on CFTR-dependent Ion Transport Activity [17]. Clinical trial name: Nasal Potential Studies Utilizing Cystic Fibrosis Transmembrane Regulator (CFTR) Modulators [20]. "
